# PDF-Only Storage & Truncated PDF Chunking Implementation Plan

This plan updates SkyVault to exclusively accept PDF files across all upload interfaces and implements a targeted chunking/extraction strategy for multi-page PDFs: when a PDF exceeds 10 pages, only the first 5 pages and the last 5 pages are extracted and chunked.

## Proposed Changes

### PDF Extraction & Chunking Strategy

#### [MODIFY] [pdf.py](file:///c:/Programs/Python/skyvault/ai_features/extractors/pdf.py)
- Inspect `len(pdf.pages)` in `extract_pdf(file_path)`.
- If `total_pages > 10`, extract text from `pdf.pages[:5]` (first 5 pages) and `pdf.pages[-5:]` (last 5 pages).
- If `total_pages <= 10`, extract text from all `pdf.pages`.
- Join extracted page texts cleanly with double newlines (`\n\n`) for downstream paragraph chunking in `chunk_text()`.
- Log page selection details (e.g., total pages and extracted range).

---

### Extractor Base & Signals Update

#### [MODIFY] [base.py](file:///c:/Programs/Python/skyvault/ai_features/extractors/base.py)
- Restrict `PDF_EXTENSIONS` to `{"pdf"}` and remove/deprecate plaintext formats from the allowlist.
- Return `None` and log a warning for any non-PDF extension.

#### [MODIFY] [signals.py](file:///c:/Programs/Python/skyvault/vault/signals.py)
- Update `TEXT_ALLOWLIST` in `vault/signals.py` to `{"pdf"}` so background AI processing (`analyze_file`) is only triggered for PDF uploads.

